<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nepal: Rescue efforts continue in the aftermath of a flash flooding disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85dfd12c2abd14450a775e8e4f48a97d0a85eabb896a2dc415f580612ae75692</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:41:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260911-nepal-rescue-efforts-continue-in-the-aftermath-of-a-flash-flooding-disaster" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the devastating flash floods, the number of dead and missing continues to rise. At Kathmandu’s public hospital, as well as outside the military base in Bidur, hundreds of photographs of missing people have been put up. Hundreds of families come forward, hoping for news – good or bad – of one or more loved ones. A race against time is underway: helping survivors, finding those still alive and identifying the victims. Rescue teams have been carrying out repeated helicopter flights, as air access is now the only way to reach remote areas cut off from the rest of the world. Civil society has also mobilised, particularly Nepal’s Generation Z. From Kathmandu to Betrawati, FRANCE 24's reporters Alban Alvarez and Fantine Dantzer accompanied a humanitarian convoy along one of the country’s most treacherous roads.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Israel says destroys Hezbollah tunnels as explosions triggers tremor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8570ff4def9f7948934223e59b348445efd3a9428ebadf1fb66340ce0d76f567</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:34:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-israel-says-destroys-hezbollah-tunnels-as-explosions-triggers-tremor" /><summary type="html">Israel said Thursday it demolished key tunnels built by the Iran-backed Hezbollah group beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, with the force of the explosions enough to trigger a 4.1 magnitude tremor. It comes a few days after Israeli authorities claimed to have taken control of the Ali al-Taher ridge, saying that the pro-Iranian Hezbollah had dug numerous tunnels there, allowing it to attack Israel from this mountainous area.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Clashing narratives': How are young Americans today taught about 9/11?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5617ec33435e83ac467896fc7945ec4d5d4c829970b95ea52449b372dbfdca42</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:24:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-clashing-narratives-how-are-young-americans-today-taught-about-9-11" /><summary type="html">An estimated 100 million Americans, almost a third of the population, were either not yet born or were too young to remember the September 11 attacks. Now, as the US marks the 25th anniversary of 9/11, how are young people in America being taught about what happened that day and its consequences? France 24's Douglas Herbert takes a look.</summary></entry><entry><title>Did the War on Terror succeed? Or did Washington fall into al Qaeda’s trap?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a403d1585a7e6fcb7a4c7b2ee6d308a18c73317f01faa4580384f70db09f136d</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:16:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260911-did-the-war-on-terror-succeed-or-did-washington-fall-into-al-qaeda-s-trap" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW: Friday, September 11– 25 years on from 9/11, the international press reflects on the war on terror, its legacy and its failings. In France, the far-right National Rally party tries desperately to distance itself from the overtly racist comments of one of its security officials, made while on duty for his day job as a police officer. Finally, a fossilised feather may give us new insights into why birds survived the asteroid that killed the dinosaurs.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Keeping the memory of 9/11 alive for the younger generation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5769ce31421d0f380fcf5f0fece63ee1de36e1f77df254b6bdeaa4f7f6125e31</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:13:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-keeping-the-memory-of-9-11-alive-for-the-younger-generation" /><summary type="html">On 11 September 2001, millions remember how they saw the World Trade Centre towers being struck by airplanes. But, 25 years after the attacks, how is the memory being passed on to the younger generation who were not around to witness them?</summary></entry><entry><title>China, Iran among countries using AI to spy on dissidents and minorities, Anthropic says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a980af4dd1544374dc3c57fa96dfba9ca2bb05a278d3598c1b6c1efda66fd63</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T07:35:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260911-anthropic-ai-surveillance-targeting-dissidents-china-iran-west-africa" /><summary type="html">Anthropic said Thursday it had disrupted several state-sponsored surveillance operations using its artificial intelligence models, warning of the growing AI use to target dissidents and minorities. The campaigns, detected between January and July, originated in China, Iran and West Africa and targeted diaspora communities, including Hong Kong pro-democracy activists.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Vance calls Democrats 'party of hatred' as he seizes MAGA spotlight</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a30db46f4a96e278eb8aa9a8a149f06ba323f49d652f16cdf078f329b5de20f</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T06:45:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-vance-tries-label-democrats-as-party-of-hatred-seizes-maga-spotlight" /><summary type="html">US Vice President JD Vance launched a virulent attack on the Democratic Party Thursday, accusing them of being the "party of hatred" at day two of the Republican convention ahead of the November midterm elections. With public support for President Donald Trump at record lows, Republican figures are increasingly trying to frame their opponents as dangerous political extremists.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lens secure an epic comeback win to kick off their Champions League campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcb8df5079656e37b96765c9542bf26b3f81fee38e2cd8bba010748ef08c0e0b</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T05:57:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260911-lens-secure-epic-comeback-win-kick-off-their-champions-league-campaign" /><summary type="html">Trailing 2-1 to Slavia Prague in the 88th minute, few could have imagined that Lens would go on to win. Yet, in just three minutes, the French side turned the game around, led by their captain Florian Thauvin.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Yemen’s Houthis seize key island in Bab al-Mandab strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3821e0f90c822fc53f7336085b64f98346b6e820119833d5b953c1acdb71dcdf</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T04:52:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260911-middle-east-live-trump-says-he-has-no-regrets-about-launching-war-on-iran" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Iran-aligned Houthi rebels took over a key island in the Red Sea, completing their push to seize control of the Bab al-Mandab strait area, a local government official and eyewitnesses said on Friday. Perim Island, also known as Mayyun, sits in the middle of the strategic waterway that links Asia to Europe. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Putin arrives in India for BRICS summit set to be dominated by Middle East, Ukraine wars</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eba1859c09ae4389bc43bd2091d5e18c2872087c01494baee3cc734854ea66ae</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T02:08:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-putin-xi-india-brics-summit-ukraine-middle-east-wars--f89644d9206b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-putin-xi-india-brics-summit-ukraine-middle-east-wars" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin arrived in New Delhi on Friday for a two-day BRICS summit expected to focus on wars in Ukraine and the Middle East and economic challenges. Putin and Iran’s President Masoud Pezeshkian are due to meet Prime Minister Narendra Modi, while China’s Xi Jinping is also expected to hold talks.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong court sentences Tiananmen vigil activists to between 5 and 7 years in jail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:462840459e25b73be5657362453ed8b2b2a59ae8af9b09fda1080cb7418cbd4b</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T01:49:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-hong-kong-court-sentences-tiananmen-vigil-activists-to-between-5-and-7-years-in-jail" /><summary type="html">Three activists who had held annual vigils commemorating the Tiananmen Square crackdown were sentenced to between five and seven years in prison Friday for calling for an "end to one-party dictatorship". Prosecutors had argued that China's constitution enshrines the primacy of the Communist Party.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Trump absent as New York marks 25 years since 9/11 with first Muslim mayor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93122fe9bd864640b7d7b0c6f0d8a7aeb1b68ccfbc679aaa406dfdcb57216119</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T01:47:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor--1ab77d9771b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor" /><summary type="html">New York on Friday marks the 25th anniversary of the September 11, 2001 attacks, with President Donald Trump set to attend a ceremony at the Pentagon while Vice President JD Vance and four former presidents join commemorations at Ground Zero, where victims’ relatives will read the names of those killed.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels seize strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d03cc7ef5a76cdfb78a5e37b4a8c6bcc2c7c74215044e677571a83ff8c506c0d</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T22:55:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran--0d8343d16cb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Houthis seized the strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha on Thursday as their offensive against Saudi-backed government forces intensified. Saudi Arabia launched dozens of airstrikes over the past 24 hours, the Houthis said, after the Iran-backed group carried out attacks on Saudi territory that wounded dozens of people.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester United thrash Sabah in Champions League return as Fabregas's Como shine in European debut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27f2811b82c352a176478f5d6ca74d951b1131958c34a06359dd1119ceeeac73</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T22:25:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260910-manchester-united-sabah-champions-league-fabregas-como-european-debut--e340158a2475.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260910-manchester-united-sabah-champions-league-fabregas-como-european-debut" /><summary type="html">Manchester United marked their Champions League return with a 4-0 rout of Sabah on Thursday, with Matheus Cunha, Bruno Fernandes, Benjamin Sesko and Lisandro Martinez scoring. Bayern Munich thrashed Bodo/Glimt 5-0 as Ballon d'Or nominees Michael Olise struck twice and Harry Kane scored, while Cesc Fabregas's Como impressed on their competition debut.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Israel destroys Hezbollah tunnel network in south Lebanon, triggering 4.1-magnitude tremor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:312b95b8f0153530f9148bc64f9f12c0f8144b54a60af2d3fec275809e38aee5</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:50:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake--c28ae45e8d7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake" /><summary type="html">Israel said on Thursday it destroyed key tunnels built by Iran-backed Hezbollah beneath the strategic Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon, completing what it called operational control of the area. Lebanon reported a massive explosion, while the US Geological Survey recorded a magnitude 4.1 tremor nearby.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Space: Europe urged to find its path, from crewed spaceflight to communications</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f3f7ddf98ed1b8fc33d5c332c957fa7a006c6a1ac952603046b1d9f420da5e6</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T21:05:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260910-space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications--2c4f857a80db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260910-space-europe-urged-to-find-its-path-from-crewed-spaceflight-to-communications" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen called on Thursday for Europeans to "act" on a massive scale to find their place against the United States and China in the space race, from communications to crewed spaceflight. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney, Svetla Ben-Itzhak, Assistant Professor of Space and International Relations, and Deputy Director of the West Space Scholars Programme at Johns Hopkins University, explains that "Europe does have world-class scientific and industrial capabilities, as well as aspirations, but it lacks the investment, the launch cadence, the scale as well as the degree of political integration that the US and China possess".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Ugandan royal succession scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:28ecdaef91ca57a05eb32243f96f437357e4e9259147b3b220f1489670b2bbcc</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:20:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ugandan-royal-succession-scandal--dc969309a6f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ugandan-royal-succession-scandal" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, a dramatic struggle for control of a throne in Uganda. Also, Rwanda shut down 101 alcoholic beverage factories last month and declared a public health crisis after at least 50 people were killed by contaminated illegal supplies. And Ethiopia celebrates its new year.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Live: Israel demolition of Hezbollah tunnels in south Lebanon caused 4.1-magnitude quake</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cce1efaaf3772abcbf9ecf447f7c8d42db8b4efd81b11a977ae334faab359ea</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:12:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain--16e2d74b863a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-middle-east-live-trump-warns-iran-not-to-get-cute-over-activity-at-pickaxe-mountain" /></entry><entry><title>Record heat and drought make this year's champagne stronger</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49decd3a04be348250a3e35f5f429ce17cb4ff4affd13552d5f465fb0e499c62</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:12:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260910-record-heat-and-drought-make-this-year-s-champagne-stronger--3cf2d8750a3d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260910-record-heat-and-drought-make-this-year-s-champagne-stronger" /><summary type="html">For the first time, French champagne producers are allowed to sell their bubbly with more than 13% alcohol, as record heatwaves and drought have resulted in grapes containing unusually high levels of sugar. They fear that climate change may eventually force them to permanently rewrite the rules governing winemaking.  Also in the segment, the European Central Bank raised interest rates for the second time this year amid higher energy costs, as a potential new gas crisis looms over Europe.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Meta tests out putting fact-checking in users’ hands across Latin America</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:110e57ad913d2b9c4943d1042a9b38672c3f4b4a124cd1884115607e0a100624</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T20:11:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1--ff193be16a97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1" /><summary type="html">Meta is expanding its shift away from professional fact-checking. The tech giant announced it's trialling it's crowdsourced "Community Notes" system across 16 countries in Latin America. Meta says the system will only fully roll out once it is confident it works, but critics warn that with misinformation, manipulated images and AI-generated content spreading rapidly, crowdsourced checks may come too late to prevent false claims from reaching millions. Vedika Bahl explains the risks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>French firefighters on six-week strike after record summer blazes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dfbda5b99e0d4d652db96b67e14a25c26e0919330ae1f2fe34e32bf134156b1c</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:41:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-firefighters-on-six-week-strike-after-record-summer-blazes--21f0641fbc58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-firefighters-on-six-week-strike-after-record-summer-blazes" /><summary type="html">Firefighters in France are on strike over a lack of funding for essential emergency services. Their dedication was pushed to the limit in the recent wild fire episodes south of Paris and near Bordeaux. Short comings in the current system were highlighted by these extreme cases. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Yael Lecras, Vice-President of the National Union of Professional Firefighters.</summary></entry><entry><title>As New York marks 25 years since 9/11, Muslims recall stigmatisation in aftermath of attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:496679d140ac715ddfb3eff1f98c2f0ddd0e9171b72264bb1dea5468c73caebf</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:32:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks--138f5fff2da5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks" /><summary type="html">As New York marks 25 years since the terrorist attacks on September 11th, New York’s Muslim community has become increasingly part of the fabric of the city. One sign of that is the election of Zohran Mamdani as the city’s mayor last November. Another is the state's largest mosque, due to open its doors at the end of the year. But while things have improved, many Muslims still remember the difficult months that followed the attack. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'No facts': Morocco denies involvement in deadly Ceuta migrant rush</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1beef649a2a0873b8845ca89de8f3e781765cea31dd3d72c1ceef2ca3b11adf6</id><updated>2026-09-11T12:53:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T19:32:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush--ae85c7241bed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260910-no-facts-morocco-denies-involvement-in-deadly-ceuta-migrant-rush" /><summary type="html">Moroccan authorities said on Thursday there were "no facts" establishing its involvement in the migrant rush into Spain's North African exclave of Ceuta in July. It was the kingdom's first official response to a Spanish police report accusing its security forces of "total permissiveness" when the mass crossing took place.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
